  "text": {
    "markdown": "## Splitting $186.40 between 4 people\n\n**With an 18% tip, each person pays $54.99.**\n\nHere is how that works out, and what other tip levels would cost:\n\n| Tip | Tip amount | Total | Per person (÷ 4) |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| No tip | $0.00 | $186.40 | $46.60 |\n| 15% | $27.96 | $214.36 | $53.59 |\n| **18%** | **$33.55** | **$219.95** | **$54.99** |\n| 20% | $37.28 | $223.68 | $55.92 |\n| 25% | $46.60 | $233.00 | $58.25 |\n\n### The 18% calculation\n\n1. Tip: $186.40 × 0.18 = $33.55\n2. Total: $186.40 + $33.55 = $219.95\n3. Per person: $219.95 ÷ 4 = $54.9875, which rounds up to **$54.99**\n\nFour payments of $54.99 come to $219.96, one cent more than the total, so the bill is fully covered.\n\n### Easier numbers\n\n- **Round up to $55 each.** That collects $220.00, and the tip becomes $33.60 (18.0%).\n- **Go to 20% and pay $56 each.** That collects $224.00; the tip is $37.60 (20.2%).\n\n### Quick mental check\n\nEach person's share of the bill before tip is $46.60. Every 5% of tip adds $2.33 per person, so 15% is about +$7, 20% is about +$9.30.\n\nTell me a different tip percentage or number of people and I will redo it. If the split should be uneven (someone skipped drinks, say), give me each person's subtotal and I will add tip proportionally.\n",
    "validation": {
      "valid": true,
      "checks": [
        "is non-empty Markdown",
        "contains no raw HTML outside code (react-markdown would print it literally)"
      ],
      "errors": [],
      "warnings": []
    }
  },
